## Variable bound twice in a pattern

```catala
declaration enumeration E:
  -- C content (integer, integer)
  -- D content (integer, integer)

declaration scope S:
  context e content E
  output o content integer

scope S:
  definition e equals C content (1, 2)
  definition o equals match e with pattern
    -- C content (x, x) or D content (x, x): x
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  The variable x is bound several times in this pattern.
│
├─➤ tests/enum/bad/or_pattern_duplicate_var.catala_en:15.22-23:
│    │
│ 15 │     -- C content (x, x) or D content (x, x): x
│    │                      ‾
├─ Variable bound twice in a pattern
│
├─➤ tests/enum/bad/or_pattern_duplicate_var.catala_en:15.19-20:
│    │
│ 15 │     -- C content (x, x) or D content (x, x): x
│    │                   ‾
└─ Variable bound twice in a pattern
#return code 123#
```
